      "content": "that's a pretty strong rebuttal. i'll use it. just out of curiosity though, do u think if a company really focuses on these social and environmental goals, they eventually stop being able to compete with companies that just go for raw profit and ignore all that stuff? like, is there a point where being \"socially responsible\" just becomes a competitive disadvantage?",
